+FIXED - cluster ci-b5ac4280f3e4b317: `ImportTrackIoTest.cpp` assigned a brace list to a `QStringList`, which Qt 5 rejects as ambiguous
+
+Verdict: **FIXED (REAL, test-source portability defect)**. The hosted
+`build / macos-arm64` job builds against Homebrew Qt 5.15
+(`/opt/homebrew/opt/qt@5/lib/QtCore.framework/Headers/qstringlist.h:111-127`), whose
+`QStringList` declares `operator=(const QList<QString> &)` and
+`operator=(QList<QString> &&)` beside its own copy/move assignments. A
+brace-enclosed list can initialise either `QStringList` or its `QList<QString>`
+base, so all four candidates are viable and overload resolution is ambiguous.
+The failure is in a first-party test source, not in CI infrastructure and not a
+product runtime bug: `zene` itself never assigns a brace list to a `QStringList`.
+
+## The reported failure
+
+Job `run-43611324689-job-132496796743`, train 050/m0-train-31 at
+`c20ef591b571e3c3dc7b108107d166497f1b34be` (this checkout's HEAD):
+
+```
+tests/src/core/ImportTrackIoTest.cpp:344:18: error: use of overloaded operator '='
+  is ambiguous (with operand types 'QStringList' and 'void')
+  note: candidate function (the implicit copy assignment operator)
+  note: candidate function (the implicit move assignment operator)
+  note: candidate function QStringList &operator=(const QList<QString> &other)
+  note: candidate function QStringList &operator=(QList<QString> &&other) noexcept
+1 error generated.
+```
+
+`tests/src/core/ImportTrackIoTest.cpp:344` is
+
+```cpp
+plan.documents = {UnparsableTrack, trackDocument(Lead)};
+```
+
+and `plan.documents` is `QStringList` (`include/ControlProjectTransplant.h:76`).
+Qt 6 defines `QStringList` as an alias of `QList<QString>`
+(`/usr/include/qt6/QtCore/qcontainerfwd.h:41`) with no extra assignment
+overloads, so this box's Qt 6 build compiles the identical line - which is why
+only the Qt 5 job failed.
+
+## Reproduction (real Qt 5.15.19 headers)
+
+The exact translation unit, compiled through its own
+`build/compile_commands.json` command line with the Qt 6 include paths replaced
